        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: load mgc with a 1 s requeue minimum",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: load mgc with a 1 s requeue minimum\n\ninit_param_vars() sets the MGC's mgc_requeue_timeout_min to 1\nsecond on every node, but each module reload puts back the\ndefault of 5, and conf-sanity reloads the modules in most of\nits subtests. A config log update then reaches a node 5 to 10\nseconds after the MGS revokes the lock rather than 1 to 2, and\nevery wait_update after a set_param -P or conf_param waits for\nit.\n\nPass the same value as a module option when the framework\nloads mgc.\n\nOn a three node ldiskfs cluster with the other open LU-20076\nchanges, the wait_update calls of conf-sanity 27b, 28a, 29,\n30a, 30b and 76d waited 38 s in all rather than 201 to 212 s,\nand 30a took 56 s rather than 172 to 189 s.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=\"27b 28a 29 30a 30b 42 76d\"\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I9c4700a7249be1b4dd892fd3cb3ffc4cfd699dd9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
